WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:03.845
Triton is the largest natural satellite of the planet Neptune.

00:04.358 --> 00:11.395
It is the only moon of Neptune massive enough to be rounded under its own gravity and hosts a thin, hazy atmosphere.

00:11.873 --> 00:22.653
Triton orbits Neptune in a retrograde orbit—revolving in the opposite direction to the parent planet's rotation—the only large moon in the Solar System to do so.

00:23.276 --> 00:30.622
Triton is thought to have once been a dwarf planet from the Kuiper belt, captured into Neptune's orbit by the latter's gravity.
